{"id":"n7e82c2307a","headline":"J&K Economy Grows, But the Exchequer Leans Harder on Delhi: CAG Audit Flags Deepening Fiscal Dependence","summary":"A CAG audit of Jammu and Kashmir reports GSDP growth of 11.18% in 2024-25. Central grants-in-aid now make up nearly 72% of revenue receipts, while own tax revenue grew just 2.5%.","why":"The Comptroller and Auditor General of India audits public finances of central and state governments. Heavy reliance on central transfers affects how fiscally self-sufficient a region is.","category":"economy","event_type":"macro-data","importance":1,"flag":null,"market_moving":false,"location":{"place":"Srinagar","country":"India","lat":34.084,"lon":74.797,"region":"asia"},"entities":[],"links":[],"source":{"name":"Kashmir Times","url":"https://kashmirtimes.com/news/jk-economy-grows-but-the-exchequer-leans-harder-on-delhi"},"sources":[{"name":"Kashmir Times","url":"https://kashmirtimes.com/news/jk-economy-grows-but-the-exchequer-leans-harder-on-delhi"}],"published_at":"2026-04-08T10:39:39Z","retrieved_at":"2026-11-17T17:30:28Z","official":false,"ai_summary":true,"content_hash":"69a1de841332d562","impacts":[],"why_moved":null,"backfilled":true,"backfilled_at":"2026-11-17T17:30:28Z","backfill_provenance":{"version":"gdelt-backfill-v1","original_published_at":"2026-04-08T10:39:39Z","feed_url":"https://data.gdeltproject.org/gdeltv2/","discovered_via":"GDELT GKG 2.1","gdelt_seen":"2026-04-08T12:00:00Z","publisher_country_gdelt":"IN","description_from":"publisher page metadata"},"image":{"kind":"topic","file":"photos/parliament-government-building-51058.jpg","alt":"parliament government building (illustration)","credit":"PeterDargatz","license":"Pixabay Content License","license_url":"https://pixabay.com/service/license-summary/","source":"Pixabay","source_url":"https://pixabay.com/photos/architecture-building-landmark-51058/"}}